WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.800
"The Batman" was filled with moments of dramatic&nbsp;
character revelations and brutal action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.440
but one scene in particular that dealt with&nbsp;
Selina Kyle's past stands out. It's time to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.000
talk about that Catwoman scene in "The Batman."
While the movie is called "The Batman," Selina&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.880
Kyle, also known as Catwoman, plays a vital role&nbsp;
in the story. Bruce Wayne first runs into her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.840
in the Iceberg Lounge, as she works for Oswald&nbsp;
Cobblepot as a server. Batman notices Selina's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.320
reaction to seeing pictures of a mystery woman&nbsp;
exiting the club with Mayor Don Mitchell Jr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.040
Batman follows Selina and discovers that the woman&nbsp;
is actually Selina's roommate. But the first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.520
they truly meet is when Selina breaks into the&nbsp;
mayor's house to retrieve her roommate's passport,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.160
and from that point on, they are entangled.
As the story unravels, more of Selina's backstory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.560
and motivations are revealed. This includes&nbsp;
a crucial connection with Carmine Falcone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.560
the mob boss who works closely with&nbsp;
Cobblepot and frequents the Iceberg Lounge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.600
When the truth of Falcone's crimes&nbsp;
comes to light thanks to the Riddler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:01:00.320
both Selina and Bruce decide to go after Falcone.
"Come on, Vengeance. Let's get into some trouble."&nbsp;

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.960
Unfortunately, Selina is a bit more serious about&nbsp;
how she wants to punish him, and Bruce doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.520
agree. But there's nothing stopping Selina&nbsp;
from going after what she wants. This leads&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.080
to a key scene in the last third of the film that&nbsp;
features major action and devastating revelations.&nbsp;

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.960
Once Selina learns that Falcone is&nbsp;
behind the death of her roommate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:21.600
she decides to kill him. Heading to his club, she&nbsp;
dresses up and asks to talk to him in private,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.280
hiding a gun in her bag. But Selina is&nbsp;
interrupted right as she reaches for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.640
the weapon. Batman is unleashing&nbsp;
his wrath in the very next room.&nbsp;

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.200
Bruce wants to stop Selina from committing murder,&nbsp;
but he also has his own business with Falcone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.640
By this point, Alfred has confirmed that&nbsp;
all signs point to Falcone ordering the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.560
murder of his parents years earlier. But&nbsp;
Bruce is forced to face off against guards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.880
and Selina gets the chance to confront Falcone.&nbsp;
She plans on getting revenge for her roommate's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.120
brutal death. She also wants answers about the&nbsp;
revelation that she's Falcone's daughter, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:53.760
apparently he doesn't know until this moment.&nbsp;
It's equally possible that he simply doesn't care.&nbsp;

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.840
Feeling like her father abandoned her years&nbsp;
earlier and knowing all of the horrors Falcone has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.880
committed, Selina pulls the trigger…and misses.&nbsp;
This leads father and daughter to battle head-on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.240
out in the open. While Selina is&nbsp;
skilled, Falcone's ruthlessness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.200
allows him to gain the upper hand.
During the confrontation at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.200
club between Falcone and Selina, she plays&nbsp;
the audio that reveals his direct role in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.800
her roommate's death. She was an innocent&nbsp;
woman who just happened to hear too much.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.280
Falcone strangles her, a detail that, only&nbsp;
minutes later, becomes even more important.&nbsp;

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.600
Selina also reminds Falcone of her mother,&nbsp;
Maria Kyle, and her death. Earlier in "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:29.360
Batman," Selina tells Bruce that her mother&nbsp;
was murdered when she was very young,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.440
likely by one of the clients at the club. While&nbsp;
Falcone first seems to feel some semblance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:37.600
emotional connection to Selina's mother's&nbsp;
name, another horrific truth comes out as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.080
Falcone attacks his daughter. He manages to knock&nbsp;
her to the ground and push down on her neck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:47.040
beginning to strangle her. It's at that point that&nbsp;
Falcone reveals that he killed Maria the same way.&nbsp;

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:51.200
If Selina hadn't managed to get away soon after,&nbsp;
she would have met the same fate as her mother.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.360
And though audiences might root for Selina&nbsp;
to take down Falcone for good, she decides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:00.000
that justice will be better served if he lives to&nbsp;
suffer the consequences of his villainy. To Bruce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.920
it means that Selina won't have to hold onto the&nbsp;
trauma that comes from taking someone's life.&nbsp;

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:08.560
In the end, while it's not by her own hand,&nbsp;
Selina does see her father die that night. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.880
the face-off with Falcone behind her, Selina&nbsp;
decides to leave Gotham City and start over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:17.920
somewhere else, something Bruce probably should&nbsp;
do as well, though we all know he never will.&nbsp;

